      "name": "addActions",
      "description": "Adds actions to a document. Prefer adding multiples actions at once to reduce the number of steps. Besides the document model's operations, accepts the base actions SET_NAME (scope global, input: the name), SET_PREFERRED_EDITOR (scope header, input: { preferredEditor }), UNDO and REDO (input: { count }) and NOOP. Returns one result per action, in input order; `success` is false when any result carries an `error`. An action its reducer rejected is stored as an operation that changes nothing, and the rest of the batch still applies. When a policy denies an action, the whole batch is refused: the denied action's error has kind `denied` and the others `not-applied`.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "documentId": {
            "description": "ID or slug of the document or drive to change. Required.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "id": {
            "description": "Alias of `documentId`",
            "type": "string"
